<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"> <channel><title>MiSTer FPGA Documentation</title><description>MiSTer FPGA is an open source project that aims to recreate various classic computers, game consoles, and arcade machines, using modern hardware.</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/</link><atom:link href="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><managingEditor>Kevin Coleman</managingEditor><docs>https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/MkDocs_MiSTer/</docs><language>en</language> <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:13:19 -0000</pubDate> <lastBuildDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:13:19 -0000</lastBuildDate> <ttl>1440</ttl> <generator>MkDocs RSS plugin - v1.15.0</generator> <image> <url>assets/mister_kun_bw.svg</url> <title>MiSTer FPGA Documentation</title><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/</link> </image> <item> <title>Saturn</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;The Sega Saturn MiSTer core, originally developed by &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.patreon.com/srg320/&#34;&gt;srg320 (Sergey Dvodnenko)&lt;/a&gt;{target=_blank}, is a suitable modern replac...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/cores/highlights/saturn/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 04 Jan 2026 20:22:44 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/cores/highlights/saturn/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/cores/highlights/saturn.png" type="image/png" length="43509" /> </item> <item> <title>Useful Snippets</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;Here are some useful HDL snippets as used throughout the MiSTer project, with sources linked for reference.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Simple Pixel Clock Divider Using Clock Enable...&lt;/h2&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/snippets/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 21 Mar 2024 17:38:53 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/snippets/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/snippets.png" type="image/png" length="48183" /> </item> <item> <title>Savestates</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;MiSTer defines a special API for fast savestate saving and loading. Enabling the savestate functionality on your core reserves a developer-specified section ...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/savestates/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 26 Apr 2023 18:34:36 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/savestates/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/savestates.png" type="image/png" length="46756" /> </item> <item> <title>Other Cores</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;This is a list of other cores in the MiSTer GitHub repository that don&#39;t fit the console or computer categories. &lt;code&gt;boot.rom&lt;/code&gt; is synonymous with &lt;code&gt;boot0.rom&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/cores/other/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 05 Apr 2023 16:25:20 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/cores/other/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/cores/other.png" type="image/png" length="48097" /> </item> <item> <title>Compiling for MiSTer</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;MiSTer combines several compiled components: a customized minimal Linux kernel, a bootloader, the Main MiSTer binary written in C, and cores built on the MiS...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/mistercompile/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 06 Sep 2022 22:56:24 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/mistercompile/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/mistercompile.png" type="image/png" length="54296" /> </item> <item> <title>MegaCD</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;The MegaCD core is a MiSTer project original developed by &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.patreon.com/srg320/&#34;&gt;srg320 (Sergey Dvodnenko)&lt;/a&gt;{target=_blank} that aims to simulate t...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/cores/highlights/megacd/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 08 Aug 2022 22:07:15 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/cores/highlights/megacd/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/cores/highlights/megacd.png" type="image/png" length="47224" /> </item> <item> <title>Video Scaling</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;MiSTer has a built-in scaler that converts the cores&#39; low-resolution video to a higher resolution, optionally using filters to improve the picture on modern ...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/videoscaling/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 15 Jul 2022 22:45:06 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/videoscaling/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/videoscaling.png" type="image/png" length="51275" /> </item> <item> <title>MRA Setnames</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;This is a list of the MRA files and the setnames used for MiSTer.ini core exceptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;| mra_filename ...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/mrasetnames/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 27 Jun 2022 02:40:15 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/mrasetnames/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/mrasetnames.png" type="image/png" length="51124" /> </item> <item> <title>Video Modes</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;#!ini video_mode&lt;/code&gt; INI setting supports several ways to specify the video mode.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Automatic Detection&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;If no &lt;code&gt;#!ini video_mode&lt;/code&gt; setting is specified, Mi...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/videomodes/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 12 Jun 2022 03:16:25 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/videomodes/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/videomodes.png" type="image/png" length="47901" /> </item> <item> <title>Core Components Where Used</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;This is a list of many recreated components used in various MiSTer FPGA cores.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;AMI&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3&gt;POKEY Sound Chip&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;[Atari 5200 &amp;amp; 800](https://github.com/MiSTer-d...&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/component/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jun 2022 18:23:09 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/component/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/component.png" type="image/png" length="57062" /> </item> <item> <title>Debugging (USB Blaster)</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;While developing a core, it&#39;s convenient to upload it through the USB Blaster (JTAG) port directly from Quartus. MiSTer supports USB Blaster and automaticall...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/debugging/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jun 2022 18:13:03 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/debugging/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/debugging.png" type="image/png" length="58041" /> </item> <item> <title>sys - arcade_video</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;arcade_video&lt;/code&gt; is used mostly in arcade cores. It provides helpers to optionally enable the scandoubler (based on ini settings), handle rotation on HDMI, and...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/arcade_video/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jun 2022 18:09:46 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/arcade_video/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/arcade_video.png" type="image/png" length="50343" /> </item> <item> <title>overview of emu module</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;On MiSTer, the top level is inside &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Template_MiSTer/blob/master/sys/sys_top.v&#34;&gt;sys/sys_top.v&lt;/a&gt;{target=_blank}. When writing or...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/emu/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jun 2022 18:09:46 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/emu/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/emu.png" type="image/png" length="51104" /> </item> <item> <title>sys - hps_io</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;HPS stands for Hard Processor System — the ARM part of the MiSTer FPGA. The &lt;code&gt;hps_io.sv&lt;/code&gt; file contains the &lt;code&gt;hps_io&lt;/code&gt; module, which talks to the MiSTer binary o...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/hps_io/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jun 2022 18:09:46 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/hps_io/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/hps_io.png" type="image/png" length="45372" /> </item> <item> <title>sys - video_freak</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;video_freak&lt;/code&gt; is used to crop and scale the image.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;video_freak&lt;/code&gt; takes the original &lt;code&gt;VGA_DE_IN&lt;/code&gt; and outputs a new &lt;code&gt;VGA_DE&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;VIDEO_ARX&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;VIDEO_ARY&lt;/code&gt; based...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/video_freak/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jun 2022 18:09:46 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/video_freak/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/video_freak.png" type="image/png" length="50072" /> </item> <item> <title>sys - video_mixer</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;video_mixer&lt;/code&gt; is a helper module that provides many of the video features the MiSTer framework supplies, including scandoubling, gamma, HQ2x scaling, and fre...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/video_mixer/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jun 2022 18:09:46 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/video_mixer/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/video_mixer.png" type="image/png" length="49840" /> </item> <item> <title>Porting Cores</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;MiSTer uses quite complex hardware, but thanks to open source, developers with different levels of hardware and software knowledge can develop for the platfo...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/porting/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jun 2022 17:47:49 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/porting/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/porting.png" type="image/png" length="49035" /> </item> <item> <title>PSX</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;The Sony PlayStation (PSX) MiSTer core is the most feature-filled and heavily developed core so far:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Multiple controller options&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Automatic BIOS region s...&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/cores/highlights/psx/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 29 May 2022 05:42:23 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/cores/highlights/psx/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/cores/highlights/psx.png" type="image/png" length="43256" /> </item> <item> <title>Core Names</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;This is a list of the core repositories and the internal core names used for MiSTer.ini core exceptions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;| Repository URL ...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/corenames/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 19 May 2022 13:25:25 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/developer/corenames/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/developer/corenames.png" type="image/png" length="48363" /> </item> <item> <title>Core Default Resolutions</title> <description>&lt;p&gt;This chart shows each core&#39;s default native resolution, frequencies, and pixel clock at startup. These values are not static and are documented for reference...&lt;/p&gt;</description><link>https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/nativeres/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 04 May 2022 16:21:26 +0000</pubDate><source url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/feed_rss_created.xml">MiSTer FPGA Documentation</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/advanced/nativeres/</guid> <enclosure url="https://mister-devel.github.io/MkDocs_MiSTer/assets/images/social/advanced/nativeres.png" type="image/png" length="55176" /> </item> </channel></rss>